  "query_preview": "..\n\nToday through Friday...\n\nAn upper level low that brought a cold front is currently moving\nover the MT/Canadian border. As a result, much cooler conditions\nand weak forcing is allowing snowfall across much of the region.\nThe greatest amounts are expected for area mountains and\nfoothills. Much of the lower elevations located west of Sheridan \nCo, WY and Bighorn Co are expected to get 4 inches or less.\nLocally higher amounts are possible along higher hills or areas\nprone to strong upslope flow. Area mountains can expect to see up\nto 6 inches of snowfall. Additional Winter Weather Advisories were\nadded across south central MT going through mid day today. Drier \nair is expected to move in mid day today, but isolated snow \nshowers may linger over the higher terrain. Use caution if \ntraveling this morning as roads may become slick from cooler \ntemperatures and accumulating snowfall. Ensembles then depict a \ncouple of weak waves to follow with ample moisture, but weak \nforcing keeps precipitation to the higher terrain across south \ncentral MT. There is good agreement between ensembles Tuesday and \nWednesday for ridging to return. Clusters are in consensus that \nridging remains in place with any potential energy and troughing \nmoving through the southwest US through the remainder of the week.\n\nTemperatures will remain below average in the upper 20s to mid 30s\nthrough Monday, returning to normal and above average (40s to low\n50s) for the latter half of the week. TS",
